family: web-ui
what: syslog
transport: udp
address: <WOODSHED-ADDRESS>
verification: reference
reference: RFC 5424 (severities, facilities), RFC 5426 (UDP), RFC 6587 (TCP), RFC 5425 (TLS)
does: The values to enter in the device's syslog (remote logging) page so it sends informational and more severe messages to Woodshed over UDP.
check: The device appears on Woodshed's Dashboard with its first message, often right after you save.
placeholders: <WOODSHED-ADDRESS>
addresses: 
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Field names differ between devices; some put the port into the address field as <WOODSHED-ADDRESS>:514.
- Pages that offer a "send a test message" button usually send it at once: watch the Dashboard.
---- part steps "": In the device's web page, open its syslog or remote logging settings and enter
Remote logging: on
Server address: <WOODSHED-ADDRESS>
Port: 514
Protocol: UDP
Lowest severity to send: informational (6)
Facility: leave the device's default
Message format: RFC 5424 if offered, otherwise the default
==== text
In the device's web page, open its syslog or remote logging settings and enter
Remote logging: on
Server address: <WOODSHED-ADDRESS>
Port: 514
Protocol: UDP
Lowest severity to send: informational (6)
Facility: leave the device's default
Message format: RFC 5424 if offered, otherwise the default
